# Pre-push CI checks

Before committing or pushing changes that touch `cpp/`, tests, or CI build config:

1. Bump version first (`powershell -File scripts\bump-version.ps1`) unless this is docs-only.
2. Run `cpp\ci-check.cmd` on Windows (or `powershell -File cpp/ci-check.ps1`).
3. Fix any failures before commit or push.
4. When adding or renaming tests, update **both**:
   - `cpp/test.ps1` (Windows CI via `test.cmd`)
   - `duskplug_tests` in `cpp/CMakeLists.txt` (Linux/macOS CI)

Windows CI uses `test.ps1`; Linux and macOS CI use CMake `duskplug_tests`. `ci-check` runs both paths so linker and source-list drift is caught locally.
